<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Odrysians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Odrysians were a Thracian people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maritsa">Hebrus</a> (Maritsa) valley in what is now southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> and European <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teres-i">Teres I</a> in the 5th century BCE they united many Thracian tribes in the Odrysian kingdom, the most powerful state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>, which drew tribute from Greek coastal cities. Odrysian kings ruled, latterly as Roman clients, until the kingdom was annexed in 46 CE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/odrysians.jpg" alt="Odrysians" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexikoua · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Odrysian.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
